11. SCIENTIFIC VISUAL QUALITY

All scientific illustrations must be consistent and readable.

For atomic models

Use correct atomic numbers.

Use correct electron configurations.

Distinguish protons, neutrons, and electrons if a nucleus is shown.

Show valence electrons clearly.

Represent electron transfer consistently.

Label ions with their correct charges.

For ion models

Distinguish cations from anions.

Display the correct charge.

Use consistent labels and colors.

Never rely on color alone to identify an ion.

For ionic crystal models

Use chemically appropriate lattice arrangements.

Use correct ion ratios.

Distinguish the unit cell from the full lattice.

Avoid presenting ionic solids as collections of discrete molecules.

Do not depict ionic attraction as an ordinary covalent bond.

For scientific equations

Use accurate formulas.

Balance chemical equations.

Use correct ionic charges.

Ensure empirical formulas correspond to electrical neutrality.

AI-generated illustrations may be used for the laboratory background, mascot, and general applications. However, atomic structures, electron configurations, chemical formulas, and crystal lattices must be generated separately using code or verified scientific models.

